WEBVTT

00:11:59.043 --> 00:12:00.082
(Laughter)

00:12:00.106 --> 00:12:01.976
It's as if they're saying,

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.987
"If you're not behaving,
I'm not going to be pro-social today."

00:12:05.011 --> 00:12:07.015
And this is what happens
without a partner,

00:12:07.039 --> 00:12:08.853
when there's no partner sitting there.

00:12:08.877 --> 00:12:12.696
So we found that the chimpanzees do care
about the well-being of somebody else --

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:15.543
especially, these are other members
of their own group.

00:12:16.175 --> 00:12:18.944
So the final experiment
that I want to mention to you

00:12:18.968 --> 00:12:20.615
is our fairness study.

00:12:20.639 --> 00:12:23.529
And so this became a very famous study.

00:12:23.553 --> 00:12:24.976
And there are now many more,

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:27.143
because after we did this
about 10 years ago,

00:12:27.167 --> 00:12:28.976
it became very well-known.

00:12:29.524 --> 00:12:31.817
And we did that originally
with capuchin monkeys.